From f43e754e21d0cb778b69993e569c4689c9fede06 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Anant Shrivastava <anant@anantshri.info>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 20:12:51 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] sycl: route BMG D=256 single-query decode to the FA
 vector kernel
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The GQA-optimized tile config has been the dispatcher's preference for
masked single-query decode since it landed. On Battlemage (bmg_g21/g31)
with head dim 256 the vector kernel is materially faster at that shape:
832 vs 1150 us per call at kv=65536, GQA4 (B70, op-level twins).

Route single-query (Q->ne[1] == 1), non-quantized-KV, max_bias == 0 decode
to BEST_FATTN_KERNEL_VEC on those parts/head sizes; every other arch, head
size, and query count keeps the existing preference. Also drop the now
redundant K->ne[1] % FATTN_KQ_STRIDE gate: the GQA-optimized TILE variant
iterates its trailing chunk out-of-bounds-checked, so n_kv no longer needs
to be a multiple of FATTN_KQ_STRIDE.

End-to-end (Arc Pro B70, llama-bench -fa 1, 2 rounds reversed order):

| cell | before | after | delta |
|---|---:|---:|---:|
| Spark-X2.5-4B BF16 tg @0 / @8k / @64k | 52.05 / 47.93 / 33.68 | 52.91 / 49.84 / 37.68 | +1.7 / +4.0 / +11.9% |
| Spark-4B-Uncensored Q8_0 tg @0 / @8k / @64k | 98.11 / 84.65 / 48.49 | 101.73 / 90.68 / 57.14 | +3.7 / +7.1 / +17.8% |
| Qwen3.8-27B Q4_K_XL tg128 @32k | 18.59 | 20.58 | +10.7% |

Prefill unchanged by construction (dispatch edit is Q->ne[1] == 1 only);
tail-arm pp cells measured flat (7603/7326/4859 vs 7603/7323/4853).

Correctness gates: FA op suite 4073/4085 — the 12 non-green are
pre-existing on the production binary (2 failures) plus 10 known >=32k-KV
tolerance overages identical across both kernels; perplexity byte-identical
between arms (14.7975 +/- 0.37670); greedy parity 4/5 byte-identical, the
5th differs only in whitespace.
