From ac3af02ebfe8eb6a1cd1ec15fa5395d5f72be5af Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Anant Shrivastava <anant@anantshri.info>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 11:29:45 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] sycl: wire GGML_SYCL_FA_TILE_DEBUG like
 GGML_SYCL_DEV_DEBUG

Address review feedback on the FA TILE dispatch instrumentation added in
this PR: it read the env var through a static-local getenv at the call
site. Follow the GGML_SYCL_DEV_DEBUG pattern instead:

- g_ggml_sycl_fa_tile_debug is a global (extern in base.hpp, defined in
  ggml-sycl.cpp), read once in ggml_check_sycl() during backend init,
  so the per-call cost on the dispatch path is one unlikely branch: no
  lazy first-call getenv and no per-template-instantiation static guard
  (fattn-tile.hpp is instantiated once per DKQ/DV combination)
- the call site in fattn-tile.hpp uses a GGML_SYCL_FA_TILE_DEBUG()
  macro shaped like GGML_SYCL_DEV_DEBUG()
- documented in docs/backend/SYCL.md (runtime env table) and echoed in
  the init "Running with Environment Variables" log alongside the other
  debug vars
---
